{"run":"dc1026","date":"2026-10-26","builds":{"ss":{"label":"superset xl-small-core","commit":"67805ac58 + patch v5 (sha256 ecfb325fb347), --io-threads-free-on-bio yes"},"lp":{"label":"superset-new-prefetch","commit":"67805ac58"},"df":{"label":"Dragonfly v2.0.2","commit":"official aarch64 release binary (tarball sha256 matches the GitHub release digest), default flags, snapshots off"},"up":{"label":"upstream Valkey","commit":"2a23bcda0"}},"instances":{"server":"c8g.metal-24xl (Graviton4), restricted with taskset to the N-core layout below","generators":"two c8g.metal-24xl hosts in the same AZ running memtier; round trips 0.11 ms and 0.23 ms, far below per-request latency in every cell","layout at N cores":"N/2 cores (min 1) for NIC IRQs, round-robin; N worker cores (Valkey: main + N-1 IO threads; Dragonfly: N proactor threads; superset's io_epoll poller also on the last worker core); one spare core for bio and jemalloc"},"method":"memtier, 128 B values, 1M keys, P1 and P16, 10 s measurement window, 3 reps per build, build order rotating per rep, server restarted per rep. 672 reps, 0 failed. Better/worse: medians more than 5% apart with no rep overlap. Latency is closed-loop client latency, median of per-second percentiles.","caveats":["Dragonfly ran with default flags and was not tuned. From 4 cores up every proactor thread is 95-100% busy, so those numbers are its CPU-bound throughput for this setup (memtier, about 2,400 connections at P16).","At 2 cores and P1 Dragonfly is unbalanced: one proactor about 99% busy, the other about 50%. Part of the 2.4-5x lead there is that imbalance, not CPU.","At 8 and 16 cores superset's io_epoll poller shares the last worker core with the last IO thread (about 50% each), and every phase barrier waits on that thread, so superset numbers there are a lower bound for this layout.","That shared core is the main reason superset trails upstream on SET P1 at 8 cores (1.01M vs 1.42M), the one cell from 4 cores up where it loses to upstream.","Upstream's IO threads sit idle at P16 because upstream is main-bound there; that is not a load-generator limit.","ENA: the NIC bandwidth allowance was exceeded in the window (MGET/MSET at P16 from 4 cores up), so the cell is a floor. IRQ: an IRQ core was above 90% busy, so the network path may be the limit."],"cells":[{"cores":2,"workload":"get","P":1,"ss":{"mops":0.4635,"reps":[0.4646,0.462,0.4635],"p50":20.607,"p99":21.311,"worker_min_busy":93,"irq":true,"ena":false},"lp":{"mops":0.4624,"reps":[0.4624,0.4602,0.4646],"p50":20.735,"p99":21.375,"worker_min_busy":93,"irq":true,"ena":false},"df":{"mops":0.1676,"reps":[0.1659,0.1688,0.1676],"p50":17.855,"p99":371.711,"worker_min_busy":50,"irq":false,"ena":false},"up":{"mops":0.3994,"reps":[0.3988,0.3994,0.4002],"p50":23.807,"p99":46.463,"worker_min_busy":100,"irq":false,"ena":false},"ss_vs_df":2.765,"ss_vs_df_verdict":"better","ss_vs_up":1.161,"ss_vs_up_verdict":"better"},{"cores":2,"workload":"set","P":1,"ss":{"mops":0.4079,"reps":[0.4077,0.4086,0.4079],"p50":23.103,"p99":25.215,"worker_min_busy":93,"irq":false,"ena":false},"lp":{"mops":0.3973,"reps":[0.3995,0.3973,0.3971],"p50":23.487,"p99":25.855,"worker_min_busy":91,"irq":false,"ena":false},"df":{"mops":0.1649,"reps":[0.1649,0.1686,0.1639],"p50":18.303,"p99":276.479,"worker_min_busy":48,"irq":false,"ena":false},"up":{"mops":0.3892,"reps":[0.39,0.3873,0.3892],"p50":24.191,"p99":39.551,"worker_min_busy":100,"irq":false,"ena":false},"ss_vs_df":2.474,"ss_vs_df_verdict":"better","ss_vs_up":1.048,"ss_vs_up_verdict":"tie"},{"cores":2,"workload":"r80w20","P":1,"ss":{"mops":0.451,"reps":[0.4492,0.451,0.4512],"p50":21.119,"p99":22.527,"worker_min_busy":94,"irq":true,"ena":false},"lp":{"mops":0.4465,"reps":[0.4461,0.4465,0.4469],"p50":21.119,"p99":22.655,"worker_min_busy":93,"irq":true,"ena":false},"df":{"mops":0.1681,"reps":[0.1696,0.1681,0.1657],"p50":18.239,"p99":296.959,"worker_min_busy":54,"irq":false,"ena":false},"up":{"mops":0.393,"reps":[0.3937,0.3928,0.393],"p50"